From 4c06c6528c2d9ab2451ddbd0936e0d3a194ece49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 06:01:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: unify GPS / Beacon / QR under locations tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Group the three location-related trigger types under a single
"ロケーション" hub with tabs (?tab=gps | beacons | qr). Existing nested
routes (/locations/new, /locations/[locationId], /locations/print) are
preserved; the dispatch happens via query parameter to avoid clashing
with [locationId].

- Shared LocationTabs component + tab config (pure helpers in .ts so
  Vitest can import without JSX)
- GpsPanel: lifted from the previous /locations page (search/sort/list/
  QR expansion all preserved)
- BeaconListPanel: extracted from /beacons/page.tsx and reused by both
  /locations?tab=beacons and the legacy /beacons route (back-compat)
- QrPanel: MVP info cards linking to existing QR touchpoints
  (locations checkin, destinations, friend-add). A note flags the
  future unified QR management screen.
- Legacy /beacons page now renders the same shared panel under the
  location tabs so both URLs land on the same UX
- Work hub card description updated to mention all three trigger types
- Tests for resolveLocationTab / isValidLocationTab / LOCATION_TABS

https://claude.ai/code/session_01SF863naiQf16RKq1NUHYwf
